 "observations": [
  "The author's own corrections are strong and were re-checked one by one; all hold. Notably 〜にとって (222168), 〜ことに (191278, 11912828), って as colloquial quotative (74880), と with 同じ/同一/比べる (139949, 218342, 235168), と as enumeration (173656, 2941019, 10270477, 126971), と as companion (3689547), と as result with なる (174090), で as cause/means/manner (11912828, 151414, 177842, 163448, 177419), に as time, frequency, purpose, result, agent and 〜うちに (148209, 187238, 126258, 195386, 163496, 96872, 10129724, 165303, 186939, 226674, 157380, 83076, 115975, 183620, 104056, 210750, 82003, 188334, 148867), も as concessive 〜ても / 〜てもいい / 何の〜も / よりも (203526, 77695, 92152, 106487, 193970, 173357, 148254, 144312), は inside なくてはならない (229825), まで as spatial limit (220261, 143822, 163448, 10659546), の as が-substitute in a relative clause (144724, 1196571) and の inside ので (140689).",
  "Ten of the twelve problems are one recurring miss and two one-offs: the author corrected the bank-modal label wherever the occurrence was clearly idiomatic, but let 'destino/direção' stand on plain existential に (12074622, 11483580, 174515, 85141) and 'inclusão (também)' stand on generalizing も with an interrogative (11788796, 10135612, 149707), even though the explanations themselves describe the right function. 237406 (神の目には) is the same kind of miss on the viewpoint に.",
  "The remaining problems are content defects, not label drift: a false statement about the て-form (91912), a citation that is not in the sentence (186348), a gloss that turns 〜に対して into cause (148082), and a non sequitur tail clause (10270477)."
 ],
